workedExamples.question_text:
Find the surface area of this sphere, correct to 2 decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) circle (1.6);
\draw (-1.6,0) arc (180:360:1.6 and 0.5);
\draw[dashed] (1.6,0) arc (0:180:1.6 and 0.5);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.2pt);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(1.6,0);
\path (0.8,0) node[below=3pt] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

This sphere has a diameter of 16 mm. Find its surface area, correct to 2 decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) circle (1.6);
\draw (-1.6,0) arc (180:360:1.6 and 0.5);
\draw[dashed] (1.6,0) arc (0:180:1.6 and 0.5);
\draw (1.75,-1.6)--(2.1,-1.6);
\draw (1.75,1.6)--(2.1,1.6);
\draw[<->] (2,-1.6)--(2,1.6);
\path (2,0) node[right=3pt] {$16\text{ mm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

